  "result": "I fixed the project limit check in `src/server/services/project-service.ts`, and the project-service tests pass (6/6). I didn't run the rest of the suite.\n\n**Cause:** when checking the limit, `createProject` asked whether adding **zero** projects would go over the plan (`wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"projects\", used, 0)`). That is only true once the organization is already over its limit. So a free organization at its limit of 2 was allowed to create a third project, and only the fourth attempt was refused.\n\n**Fix:**\n- The check now counts the project being created (it uses the default of 1).\n- The error message had the same problem. It printed the number of projects the organization had, not the plan's limit. It now shows the limit.\n\nThe create-project server action (`src/actions/projects/create-project.ts`) already compared usage with `>=`, which was correct. The wrong check in the service was letting the extra project through.",
